  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only result is scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (0.653 acc, config_006), and image-only resnet50 single-profile is very weak (0.208 acc, config_010). The critical open question is whether adding the image modality to the strongest RNA pipeline yields any complementary signal, or whether the weak image performance (0.208) means fusion will be neutral-to-harmful. Config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) directly tests this by taking the proven best RNA configuration and adding image with the simplest fusion (concat). This is the most informative next step because: (1) it exploits the strongest known RNA setup, (2) it answers the highest-uncertainty design question—does multimodal help at all in this task—before spending budget on more complex fusion variants or alternative image encoders, and (3) the result will determine whether subsequent experiments should invest in multimodal exploration (ViT, weighted fusion) or refocus on RNA-only refinements."
}

